//! The `font-synthesis` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS)
//! [shorthand](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Shorthand_properties)
//! property lets you specify whether or not the browser may synthesize the bold, italic, small-caps,
//! and/or subscript and superscript typefaces when they are missing in the specified font-family.
//!
//! Initial: weight style small-caps position . Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - none: Indicates that no bold, italic, or small-caps typeface may be synthesized by the browser.
//! - position: Indicates that the subscript and superscript typeface may be synthesized by the
//! browser, if needed, when using `font-variant-position`.
//! - small-caps: Indicates that the small-caps typeface may be synthesized by the browser if needed.
//! - style: Indicates that the italic typeface may be synthesized by the browser if needed.
//! - weight: Indicates that the missing bold typeface may be synthesized by the browser if needed.
//!
//! Grammar: none | [ weight || style || small-caps || position]
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4/#propdef-font-synthesis
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/font-synthesis
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

